{
  "module": "floaters",
  "title": "What Are Those Squiggles Floating in Your Eyes?",
  "music": "ambient",
  "length_scale": 1.08,
  "punch": 0.06,
  "max_clip": 2.6,
  "shots": [
    {
      "vo": "What are those little squiggles floating in your vision?",
      "highlight": "#7fd8ff",
      "scene": "pov",
      "params": {"n": 7},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "floating", "scene": "eye", "params": {"clump0": 1, "clump1": 1, "slosh": 1, "dist0": 26, "dist1": 22}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "Your eyeball is filled with a clear jelly called the vitreous.",
      "highlight": "#7fd8ff",
      "scene": "eye",
      "params": {"fibers": 0, "az0": 0.9, "az1": 0.6, "dist0": 24, "dist1": 21},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "jelly", "params": {"fibers": 0, "labels": 1, "az0": 0.2, "az1": 0.1}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "It's mostly water, held together by tiny fibers of collagen.",
      "highlight": "#7fd8ff",
      "scene": "eye",
      "params": {"fibers": 1, "az0": -0.3, "az1": -0.1},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "fibers", "params": {"fibers": 1, "az0": 0.3, "az1": 0.45, "dist0": 11, "dist1": 9, "tx0": -0.6, "tx1": -0.6, "tz0": -1, "tz1": -1}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "Over time, some of those fibers clump together.",
      "highlight": "#ffd23f",
      "scene": "eye",
      "params": {"clump0": 0, "clump1": 0.5, "dist0": 13, "dist1": 11, "tz0": -0.8, "tz1": -0.8},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "clump", "params": {"clump0": 0.5, "clump1": 1, "az0": 0.6, "az1": 0.45, "dist0": 9, "dist1": 8, "tx0": -0.6, "tx1": -0.6, "tz0": -0.8, "tz1": -0.8}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "When light comes in, the clumps cast shadows on your retina.",
      "highlight": "#ffd23f",
      "scene": "eye",
      "params": {"clump0": 1, "clump1": 1, "rays": 1, "dist0": 24, "dist1": 21},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "shadows", "params": {"clump0": 1, "clump1": 1, "rays": 1, "shadows": 1, "az0": 1.1, "az1": 0.9, "el0": 0.1, "el1": 0.05, "dist0": 10, "dist1": 9, "tx0": -1.5, "tx1": -1.6, "tz0": -0.6, "tz1": -0.6}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "That's what you see. They drift because the jelly sloshes every time your eye moves.",
      "highlight": "#7fd8ff",
      "scene": "pov",
      "params": {"n": 9},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "jelly", "scene": "eye", "params": {"clump0": 1, "clump1": 1, "slosh": 1, "rays": 1, "shadows": 1, "dist0": 20, "dist1": 18}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "Floaters are usually harmless. But a sudden shower of new ones, or flashes of light, can mean a torn retina.",
      "highlight": "#ff4b4b",
      "scene": "pov",
      "params": {"n": 5},
      "cuts": [
        {"at": "shower", "scene": "pov", "params": {"n": 6, "shower": 1}},
        {"at": "flashes", "scene": "pov", "params": {"n": 6, "shower": 1, "flash": 1}},
        {"at": "torn", "scene": "retina", "params": {"tear0": 0.2, "tear1": 1, "flash": 1}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "vo": "That needs an eye doctor the same day.",
      "highlight": "#ff4b4b",
      "scene": "retina",
      "params": {"tear0": 1, "tear1": 1, "az0": 0.4, "az1": 0.3, "dist0": 14, "dist1": 16}
    }
  ]
}
